feat(roadmap): link claims to sessions + agents (ADR-0034) (#97)

* feat(roadmap): link claims to sessions + agents (ADR-0034)

Closes the seam between roadmap_claims and the existing sessions/agents
tables. Before this, a claim said `claimed_by: "agent-foo"` and that
string was a coordination receipt but not a join key — `pd sessions`
couldn't say "this session is working on slug X", and a future
`pd whois <slug>` had nothing to resolve.

Schema:
  ALTER TABLE roadmap_claims ADD COLUMN session_id TEXT;
  ALTER TABLE roadmap_claims ADD COLUMN agent_id   TEXT;
  CREATE INDEX idx_roadmap_claims_session
    ON roadmap_claims(session_id) WHERE session_id IS NOT NULL;

Migration is idempotent (PRAGMA table_info gate). Pre-ADR-0034 databases
get the columns backfilled with NULL; existing claims stay valid.

Surfaces:
  POST /cartographer/roadmap-pop          now accepts sessionId, agentId
  POST /cartographer/roadmap-claim-link   new — write or rebind a link
                                           (idempotent, refuses to
                                           overwrite without force:true)

CLI:
  pd roadmap pop --begin                  now writes session+agent back
                                           onto the claim row after the
                                           pd begin chain returns
  pd roadmap claim-link <slug>            new — manual rebind verb
    [--session <id>] [--agent <id>] [--force]
  pd roadmap claims                       output now includes
                                           "session: <id>" line

Module:
  lib/roadmap-pop.ts grows linkClaim() and getClaimBySession() while
  keeping pop()/release()/listClaims()/getActiveClaim() unchanged in
  shape. PopOptions accepts optional sessionId/agentId.

10 new unit tests cover: pop-with-link, pop-without-link, link by
claimId, link by slug, refuse-overwrite, --force rebind, idempotent
no-op, no-active-claim (unknown + released), missing-args, reverse
lookup by session, and the migration path on a pre-ADR-0034 database.
57/57 in the suite pass, including the prior 21 and adjacent
cartographer-routes / manifest-enforcement tests.

CHANGELOG entry rolls into the existing proposed-3.15.0 minor. Manifest
declares the new route.

This is step 1 of the seam Erich asked about. Step 2 (claim ↔ file
predictions via roadmap_claim_files + cartographer/symbol-index) is a
separate ADR; this one stops at session linkage because that's the
minimum bar to make pd sessions / pd whois useful and avoids dragging
in the prediction pipeline.

* fix(roadmap-link): preserve unspecified column in linkClaim

Two Copilot findings on PR #97:

1. `linkStmt` wrote both columns unconditionally, so
   `linkClaim({ sessionId: 'new' })` on a row with `agent_id = 'A1'`
   silently overwrote `agent_id` to NULL. That's a real bug, not just a
   linting issue — partial updates are the common path (CLI fills
   session first, agent later). Switched to `SET session_id =
   COALESCE(?, session_id), agent_id = COALESCE(?, agent_id)` so NULL
   from the caller means "leave this column alone."

2. Dead `sameSession` / `sameAgent` variables in linkClaim were
   misleading — `(sessionId === null && row.session_id !== null)`
   reads as the *clear* condition, not a *sameness* check, and
   `requestMatchesExisting` already encapsulated the real decision.
   Replaced with the post-merge `wouldBecome` projection plus
   `noChange` / `wouldOverwrite` predicates that match what the SQL
   will actually do.

New test: `linkClaim preserves the other column when only one is
passed`. Asserts that updating session leaves the prior agent
untouched. 33/33 in the suite pass.

